etween Sweden and Norway 1814–1905","inception":1814.841095890411,"dissolved":1905.4301369863015,"enwiki":"Union between Sweden and Norway","summary":"Sweden and Norway or Sweden–Norway (Swedish: Svensk-norska unionen; Norwegian: Den svensk-norske union(en)), officially the United Kingdoms of Sweden and Norway, and known as the United Kingdoms, was a personal union of the separate kingdoms of Sweden and Norway under a common monarch and common foreign policy that lasted from 1814 until its peaceful dissolution in 1905.\nThe two states kept separate constitutions, laws, legislatures, administrations, state churches, armed forces, and currencies; the kings mostly resided in Stockholm, where foreign diplomatic representations were located. The Norwegian government was presided over by viceroys: Swedes until 1829, Norwegians until 1856. That office was later vacant and then abolished in 1873."}],"facts":[{"qid":"Q62589","kind":"capital","value_qid":"Q1754","value_label":"Stockholm","from_t":null,"to_t":null,"title":null,"property":"P36","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Stockholm"},{"qid":"Q62589","kind":"capital","value_qid":"Q21711493","value_label":"Christiania","from_t":null,"to_t":null,"title":null,"property":"P36","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Christiania"},{"qid":"Q62589","kind":"official_language","value_qid":"Q9027","value_label":"Swedish","from_t":null,"to_t":null,"title":null,"property":"P37","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Swedish"},{"qid":"Q62589","kind":"official_language","value_qid":"Q9043","value_label":"Norwegian","from_t":null,"to_t":null,"title":null,"property":"P37","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Norwegian"},{"qid":"Q62589","kind":"language","value_qid":"Q56463","value_label":"Sámi","from_t":null,"to_t":null,"title":null,"property":"P2936","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Sámi"},{"qid":"Q62589","kind":"language","value_qid":"Q9027","value_label":"Swedish","from_t":null,"to_t":null,"title":null,"property":"P2936","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Swedish"},{